    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T14:04:54Z",
    "body": "Stopped after the second gate attempt.\n\nThe waterjet implementation is held locally in .claude/worktrees/issue-1881 on branch issue/1881-waterjet-kinds.\nThe branch starts at PR #1811 head 73b64e71fc1f6259f247537d1c61d64db4ed304f.\nThe changes are not committed or pushed.\n\nThe first parser pin failed on unchanged code because waterjet was an unknown machine kind.\nAll 28 new issue pins now pass.\nAll 69 behavioral mutation checks failed with the mutation and passed after restoration.\nTwo of those checks restored actual upstream files before restoring the fix.\nThe workspace all-targets compile check passed.\nClippy passed with -D warnings for camcraft-app, camcraft-post, camcraft-tools and camcraft-ui.\n\nThe first full quick gate found an outdated allowed-kind assertion and a shared tool icon.\nBoth are fixed and their targeted tests pass.\nThe waterjet now has an original SVG master and its own product icon.\nThe icon master check passes.\n\nThe second quick gate, restricted to the remaining UI step, fails only headless_run_succeeds and headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero.\nBoth fail because wgpu reports no graphics adapter.\nMetal exposes no adapter in this environment and has no software fallback here.\nNo GPU tests were skipped or weakened.\n\nThis issue changes no NC or CL golden.\nThe 21 direct upstream golden differences all match the unchanged #1811 stack parent.\n\nI am releasing the claim under the requested two-failure stop rule.\nA session with a graphics adapter can resume the local worktree, finish validation and open the draft PR.\n",
