    "body": "Stopped under the requested two-failure gate rule. I am releasing the claim.\n\nThe staged implementation remains uncommitted in .claude/worktrees/issue-1881 on branch issue/1881-waterjet-kinds.\nThe worktree is in /home/mikekinney/CamcraftCodex.\nIt starts from upstream/main 3580f388821d604e602728495a53df1881889b0d.\nNothing was pushed. No PR was opened.\n\nThe first parser pin failed on unchanged code because waterjet was an unknown machine kind.\nThe patch adds machine and tool kinds, recipe data, file roundtrips, XY machine checks, and UI tool support.\nIt admits only the waterjet family on a waterjet machine.\nNo concrete waterjet operation or built-in waterjet post exists in this slice.\n\nThe targeted suites pass: five post tests, six tools tests, thirteen app integration tests, one private post test, and two new UI tests.\nThe existing tool-icon test and four tool-law tests also pass.\nAll 74 behavioral mutations failed at runtime with the mutation and passed after restoration.\nFour replays with actual upstream source files also failed and then passed after restoration.\nEvery mutated source file was restored.\nThe UI all-targets compile check and icon-master check pass.\nNo NC or CL golden changed.\n\nQuick gate attempt 1 passed tools, post, and UI, including the GPU and headless tests.\nIts app step failed to compile because tool_law.rs lacked the new exhaustive enum arm.\nThe first Clippy run also found type_complexity in a new post test fixture.\nBoth test-only findings were corrected. Their targeted tests pass.\n\nQuick gate attempt 2 failed machine_library::other_stated_values_refuse_by_name.\nThat existing test expects \"not mill, lathe, mill-turn or plasma\".\nThe validator now says \"not mill, lathe, mill-turn, plasma, waterjet, wire_edm or sinker_edm\".\nI stopped without changing that assertion, as requested.\nThe second gate was interrupted after this failure. Clippy was not rerun after the fixture correction.\n\nEvidence remains outside the branch in /tmp/1881-quick2.txt, /tmp/1881-clippy.txt, and /tmp/1881-* mutation and pin logs.\nSelf-review, the decision record, commit, push, and draft PR remain undone.\nThe claim is released so another session can resume the held work.\n",
